{"name":"Black Chasm","hex":"#102c33","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"black","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Absorbing all light and reflecting none; dark and hueless.","Without light."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour/color perceived in the absence of light, but also when no light is reflected, but rather absorbed.","A black dye or pigment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black"},{"term":"chasm","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep, steep-sided rift, gap or fissure; a gorge or abyss.","A large difference of opinion."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chasm"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rift","blocks":[{"text":"In geology, a rift is a linear zone where the lithosphere is being pulled apart and is an example of extensional tectonics. Typical rift features are a central linear downfaulted depression, called a graben, or more commonly a half-graben with normal faulting and rift-flank uplifts mainly on one side. Where rifts remain above sea level they form a rift valley, which may be filled by water forming a rift lake. The axis of the rift area may contain volcanic rocks, and active volcanism is a part of many, but not all, active rift systems."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Rift_segmentation.png/330px-Rift_segmentation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rift"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/GulfofSuezRift.png/500px-GulfofSuezRift.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/GulfofSuezRift.png/1280px-GulfofSuezRift.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/GulfofSuezRift.png/500px-GulfofSuezRift.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gulf of Suez Rift showing main extensional faults","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGulfofSuezRift.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/FlankMalawi.png/500px-FlankMalawi.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/FlankMalawi.png/1280px-FlankMalawi.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/FlankMalawi.png/500px-FlankMalawi.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Topographic profile of Lake Malawi","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlankMalawi.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/20190621_CPH-KEF_7314_%2848453477346%29.jpg/500px-20190621_CPH-KEF_7314_%2848453477346%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/20190621_CPH-KEF_7314_%2848453477346%29.jpg/1280px-20190621_CPH-KEF_7314_%2848453